  "arxiv_id": "2601.12164",
  "title": "The Language You Ask In: Language-Conditioned Ideological Divergence in LLM Analysis of Contested Political Documents",
  "summary": "Replaces single-language neutrality evaluation with semantically paired prompts in different languages. It needs paired prompts and extra API calls, with human interpretation because contested questions lack a definitive answer key. The study reports that ChatGPT 5.2 and Claude Opus 4.5 adopt the prompt language's dominant framing, but examines a single Ukrainian document and does not establish generalization to other language pairs or topics.",
  "rationale": "An inexpensive API-based evaluation for multilingual products handling sensitive content, but the single-document finding needs validation in the reader's domain.",
  "technique": "Prompt-language-conditioned ideological bias evaluation",
